From 2ac15656ea598a5e6bafabd44893a8e834920e6a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 09:48:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] verify: the last stage draws a batch window's sampled
 rows right behind its graph (opt-in STRATA_EARLY_SAMPLE=1)

batch_launch enqueues sample_rows' per-row sample_tokens launches on cs_ behind the window and its commit, in
sample_rows' order, so batch_poll finds them done instead of launching them and waiting (cudaStreamSynchronize)
after it has seen the graph finish.  Same kernels, same logits, same Philox(seed, position), same stream order:
the same tokens.  batch_poll still draws a row when its draw would differ from the early one (same_sampling: every
field sample_tokens reads, floats bit for bit), and rows with a logit bias are always drawn there.  init_slots takes
the split sampler's scratch beforehand (sample_tokens_reserve), so no cudaMalloc runs with the window in flight and
the split never falls back to the one-block kernel there.  Greedy rows are unchanged (their pick is the graph's).
Off by default: nothing changes; SASS of every .cu object is identical.  sampler_same_test (CPU) covers
same_sampling.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
